## Agent Orchestration

Use event-driven coordination.

Example event:

DoctorDelayed.

Expected workflow:

1. Doctor availability changes.
2. Queue prediction service recalculates ETAs.
3. Scheduling agent identifies affected appointments.
4. Notification workflow prepares patient updates.
5. Reception dashboard receives alerts.
6. Admin dashboard updates operational metrics.
7. Authorized staff approve actions when required.

Agents must not directly modify the database outside validated application services.

Use structured tool calls.

Validate all tool arguments.

Apply authorization and patient access checks.

Log agent actions.

Require human approval for sensitive operations.

